{"body":"Requesting changes here before this can merge. Three issues below need to be addressed, and I've left more detailed feedback inline for a few other items worth a look.

**1. When every colour is sold out, the page shows the wrong thing.** Left a comment on the exact line, but here's what's happening: there's a flag called `suppressColourAttribute` that's supposed to turn off the old colour picker whenever your new one takes over. But when every colour is unavailable, that flag flips back to false, so the old picker turns back on, and it shows every unavailable colour as a greyed out square instead of just showing nothing. There's no product in the current test catalogue where every colour is actually unavailable, so I couldn't click through this live. I wrote a quick script instead, using the real logic from both files, to run it against a made up product with everything unavailable and confirm the mechanism directly. Happy to share it if useful.

**2. The new Playwright tests don't actually run.** The test file calls five functions to get test products (`pdpProductWithMultipleColours` and four others) that don't exist anywhere in the fixtures file, and it also expects around ten things on the `ProductPage` helper that were never added. I ran the tests against a real dev server just to check: all 11 failed, none of them skipped. They're written well otherwise, once the missing pieces exist they should actually catch real bugs, but I'm not sure what the value is in including 11 tests in a PR when none of them can currently run or be verified. Might be worth updating the PR description too, since right now it says all 11 are skipping because of missing test data, and that's not what's happening.

**3. Colour swatches turned into squares everywhere, not just on this page.** There's a line in `product-view` that used to pick circle or square depending on the attribute, and now it's just always square, and it's not wrapped in the same check that turns off the old picker. So cart, wishlist, and bonus product all get square swatches now too, not just this PDP. I checked the cart's edit modal and yeah, it's square there now. This styles things well outside the scope of the colour swatch on this PDP, and it's actually wrong for those other places too, the expanded gallery for example uses rounded colour swatches by design, so this breaks that. Changes here should stay scoped to just this page's colour swatch, not touch the shared component's default behaviour.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","submitted_at":"2026-08-31T17:15:45Z"}
